<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 12th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 1100s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/12th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 1150 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10576 5566" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 1150 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="6134" cy="1224" r="180"/><text x="6134" y="1300" font-size="216">1</text></g><g><circle cx="8012" cy="829" r="180"/><text x="8012" y="905" font-size="216">2</text></g><g><circle cx="5709" cy="970" r="180"/><text x="5709" y="1046" font-size="216">3</text></g><g><circle cx="5229" cy="694" r="180"/><text x="5229" y="770" font-size="216">4</text></g><g><circle cx="7846" cy="1933" r="180"/><text x="7846" y="2009" font-size="216">5</text></g><g><circle cx="4794" cy="1282" r="180"/><text x="4794" y="1358" font-size="216">6</text></g><g><circle cx="6748" cy="1217" r="180"/><text x="6748" y="1292" font-size="216">7</text></g><g><circle cx="7088" cy="1770" r="180"/><text x="7088" y="1846" font-size="216">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 1150 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Abbasid Caliphate &middot; Khmer Empire &middot; Almohad Caliphate &middot; Western Chalukya Empire &middot; Jin dynasty (1115-1234) &middot; Byzantine Empire &middot; Ghaznavid Empire &middot; Holy Roman Empire</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Alarcos</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Ourique</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Legnano</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Treaty of Zamora</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Third Crusade</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Second Crusade</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Frederick Barbarossa</li><li>John, King of England</li><li>Henry the Lion</li><li>Henry II of England</li><li>Richard I of England</li><li>Andrei Bogolyubsky</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1122–1190</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1166–1216</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 1129–1195</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 1111–1174</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1157–1199</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1133–1189</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 1100s, 296 recorded states were founded and 150 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Abbasid Caliphate, the Jin dynasty (1115-1234) and the Byzantine Empire. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 12th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/12th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 12th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Abbasid Caliphate <span>750 CE – 1517 CE</span></li><li>Jin dynasty (1115-1234) <span>1115 CE – 1234 CE</span></li><li>Byzantine Empire <span>330 CE – 1453 CE</span></li><li>Holy Roman Empire <span>800 CE – 1806 CE</span></li><li>Khmer Empire <span>802 CE – 1431 CE</span></li><li>Almohad Caliphate <span>1121 CE – 1269 CE</span></li><li>Ghaznavid Empire <span>977 CE – 1186 CE</span></li><li>Western Chalukya Empire <span>973 CE – 1189 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Battle of Ourique <span>1139</span></li><li>Treaty of Zamora <span>1143</span></li><li>Second Crusade <span>1147–1149</span></li><li>Battle of Legnano <span>1176</span></li><li>Third Crusade <span>1189–1192</span></li><li>Battle of Alarcos <span>1195</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Frederick Barbarossa <span>1: 1122–1190</span></li><li>John, King of England <span>2: 1166–1216</span></li><li>Henry the Lion <span>3: c. 1129–1195</span></li><li>Henry II of England <span>6: 1133–1189</span></li><li>Richard I of England <span>5: 1157–1199</span></li><li>Andrei Bogolyubsky <span>4: c. 1111–1174</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
